"""
ur3e_pick_all.py  -  Track B (single file: scene builder + vision + PBVS + controller): vision-guided pick with a UR3e in MuJoCo (PBVS)

Pipeline per trial
  1. robot goes to an observation pose (tool pointing down, camera over the table)
  2. wrist RGB-D image -> red-cube segmentation (HSV) -> depth-based 3D position
     (calibrated intrinsics + known camera pose)
  3. position-based visual servoing: pre-grasp -> straight-line descent -> grasp -> lift,
     joint references from damped-least-squares IK (mj_jacSite)
  4. joints are driven by a state-space controller:
        - each joint is a double integrator after computed-torque linearisation
        - full-state feedback  u = -K (x_hat - x_ref) + a_ref   (pole placement)
        - Luenberger observer estimates [q, qdot] from noisy q only
Cube (x, y) is randomised every trial; detection / localisation / pick rates are logged.

Usage:   python ur3e_pick_all.py                 (opens the MuJoCo viewer, 5 trials)
         python ur3e_pick_all.py --headless --trials 100   (fast batch run for the statistics)
Output:  stage3_output/  (trials.csv, detection images, trial-0 signals)
"""
